1
00:04:13,636 --> 00:04:19,636
Persuasion is a drama, romance, tv movie film directed by Adrian Shergold.

2
00:08:27,272 --> 00:08:33,272
Living with her snobby family on the brink of bankruptcy, Anne Elliot
is an unconforming woman with modern sensibilities.

3
00:12:40,909 --> 00:12:46,909
When Frederick Wentworth – the dashing one she once sent away – crashes back into her life, Anne must choose
between putting the past behind her or listening to her heart when it comes to second chances.

4
00:16:54,545 --> 00:17:00,545
Anne Elliot, played by Sally Hawkins.

5
00:21:08,181 --> 00:21:14,181
Captain Wentworth, played by Rupert Penry-Jones.

6
00:25:21,818 --> 00:25:27,818
Lady Russell, played by Alice Krige.

7
00:29:35,454 --> 00:29:41,454
William Elliot, played by Tobias Menzies.

8
00:33:49,090 --> 00:33:55,090
Sir Walter Elliot, played by Anthony Stewart Head.

9
00:38:02,727 --> 00:38:08,727
Elizabeth Elliot, played by Julia Davis.

10
00:42:16,363 --> 00:42:22,363
Persuasion is a 2007 British historical romance television film
adaptation of Jane Austen's 1817 novel Persuasion.

11
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
It was directed by Adrian Shergold, and the
screenplay was written by Simon Burke.

12
00:50:43,636 --> 00:50:49,636
Sally Hawkins stars as the protagonist Anne Elliot, while Rupert
Penry-Jones plays Captain Frederick Wentworth.

13
00:54:57,272 --> 00:55:03,272
Eight years before the film's beginning, Anne was persuaded
to reject Wentworth's proposal of marriage.

14
00:59:10,909 --> 00:59:16,909
Now 27 and unmarried, Anne re-encounters Wentworth, who has made his fortune in the Napoleonic Wars and is
looking for a wife—anyone but Anne, whom he has not forgiven for rejecting him all those years ago.

15
01:03:24,545 --> 01:03:30,545
Persuasion was one of three novels adapted in 2007 for ITV's Jane Austen Season.

16
01:07:38,181 --> 01:07:44,181
It was the first of the three adaptations to begin development.

17
01:11:51,818 --> 01:11:57,818
The drama was co-produced by Clerkenwell Films and American studio WGBH Boston.

18
01:16:05,454 --> 01:16:11,454
Persuasion premiered on 1 April 2007 in the United Kingdom
and was watched by 5.4 million viewers.

19
01:20:19,090 --> 01:20:25,090
Persuasion received positive reviews from television critics.

20
01:24:32,727 --> 01:24:38,727
The film explores themes of navy, based on novel or
book, love triangle, poetry, love.

21
01:28:46,363 --> 01:28:52,363
The tone is emotional.
